  "id": "COMPOUND:34528 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound [(1S,2S,3R,4R,6S,7S,8R,11R,13S,15S)-11-acetyl-7,13-dihydroxy-4,8-dimethyl-14-methylidene-10-oxo-9,16-dioxapentacyclo[6.6.1.12,6.02,6.011,15]hexadecan-3-yl] (2S)-2-methylbutanoate and DNA polymerase iota, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that interact with this enzyme. Specifically, the compound is a target of Bezerramycin B, Sophorabioside, and 1,3a-Ethano-3aH-indene, all of which are known to interact with DNA polymerase iota. This indicates that the compound may exert its effects through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a known target of these compounds. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of DNA polymerase iota, potentially influencing its function in processes such as DNA replication and repair. The strength of the evidence is supported by multiple independent pathways, but the exact mechanism by which the compound interacts with DNA polymerase iota remains to be fully elucidated.",
